-# Chronyx Mobile 0.1.0-alpha.1
+# Chronyx Mobile 0.2.0-alpha.2
 
 Native Android browser shell derived from the verified Chronyx Desktop 0.7.0-alpha.37 product/security baseline. Android does not run the Electron desktop architecture; this build intentionally uses the device's updatable Chromium-based Android WebView instead of emulating or exposing Electron APIs.
 
 ## Included
 
 - Dark Chronyx mobile chrome with resize-safe Android system insets.
-- Up to 8 live tabs, explicit WebView destruction on tab close, crash recovery, tab restore across restart.
+- Up to 12 live tabs, explicit WebView destruction on tab close, crash recovery, tab restore across restart.
 - HTTPS-first address/search resolution with DuckDuckGo fallback and blocking of arbitrary privileged/custom schemes.
-- ChatGPT shortcut/home, standard browser navigation, Android default-browser VIEW intents.
+- Personal-browser home page (DuckDuckGo by default), editable home URL, ChatGPT shortcut, standard navigation and Android default-browser VIEW intents.
+- Persistent bookmarks, bounded history and recently closed tabs with reopen support.
+- User-gesture `target=_blank` / popup handling in real Chronyx tabs.
+- Per-tab Desktop Site mode using the installed WebView Chromium major version rather than a fabricated browser version.
 - Android Safe Browsing enabled; SSL certificate errors are never bypassed.
 - No `addJavascriptInterface` or JavaScript-to-native privileged bridge.
 - `file://` access disabled for remote WebViews; mixed content disabled.
